# Phase 55: Google GenAI Migration

## Goal Description
Migrate all remaining Python files from the legacy `google-generativeai` (v0.x) library to the modernized `google-genai` (v1.0+) library. This unifies the codebase on a single, robust client (DualEngineLLM) and eliminates technical debt.

## Proposed Changes

### 1. Core Providers (Critical)
**Goal:** Migrate foundational logic used by the entire app.
- [x] [providers/gemini.py](file:///Users/lokeshgarg/ai-mvp-backend/providers/gemini.py) (Main LLM provider)
- [x] [providers/embeddings.py](file:///Users/lokeshgarg/ai-mvp-backend/providers/embeddings.py) (Vector ops)
- [x] [providers/memory.py](file:///Users/lokeshgarg/ai-mvp-backend/providers/memory.py) (Memory context)
- [x] [providers/safety.py](file:///Users/lokeshgarg/ai-mvp-backend/providers/safety.py) (Safety filters)

### 2. Nucleus Runtime (Critical)
**Goal:** Clean up the "Dual Engine" adapter to be "Single Engine" (V1 native).
- [x] [mcp_server_nucleus/runtime/llm_client.py](file:///Users/lokeshgarg/ai-mvp-backend/mcp-server-nucleus/src/mcp_server_nucleus/runtime/llm_client.py) (Remove legacy fallbacks)

